course: dictionary
lesson: 13688
title: Born with it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some things you can do because you practised them, like riding a bike. Other things you seem to have from the start. The word innate describes those. Innate means something you are born with, not something you learned. «The spider spins its web without anyone teaching it, so its skill is innate.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «Lily has an innate talent for drawing; she was sketching animals before she could hold a pencil properly», the words before she could hold a pencil show the talent was there from the start. So innate must mean born with it.
explain: Innate can also mean a natural part of something. «Curiosity is innate in most children; they want to ask why.» Here the word tells us curiosity is part of being a child, not something that was taught. Check your meaning by swapping it in: born with it, not learned, still makes sense.
fact: Innate means born with it, not learned.
fact: An innate talent is a skill you seem to have from birth, like a natural gift for music.
fact: Instincts are innate: a spider spins a web without being taught.
fact: In science, innate behaviour is something an animal does without learning it first.
fact: Nature vs nurture is a debate about whether our abilities are innate or learned from the people and places around us.
exercise: «The spider spins its web without being taught. Its skill is innate.» What does innate mean? | *Born with it, not learned | Something you can buy in a shop | Very fast | Learned from a teacher
exercise: «Lily has an innate talent for drawing.» What does this tell you about Lily's talent? | It is only for special days | She practised it for years at school | She borrowed it from her friend | *She was born with it
exercise: Which word is the opposite of innate, meaning something you get by practice? | Natural | *Learned | Instinctive | Born with it
test: «Her innate kindness made everyone smile.» What does innate suggest about her kindness? | It is something she bought | It was taught to her in school | *It is part of who she is, not learned | It only shows up on birthdays
test: Which sentence uses innate correctly? | The cake was innate | The bus was innate and late | *Puppies have an innate urge to chew | Innate, I went to the shop
exam: Dan says the spider's web-spinning is innate, so someone must have taught it. Is Dan right? | No, because spiders cannot spin | Yes, because spiders go to school | Yes, all skills are taught | *No, innate means born with it, not taught
